# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Bright OS - labwc experimental session packages
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Phase 6.1 proof-of-concept. This list is NOT pulled into the default ISO
# (it is NOT referenced from core.list.chroot or any edition list). It
# exists to document the packages needed to enable the experimental
# 'bright-labwc.desktop' wayland session, and will be promoted to core
# once labwc passes the PoC acceptance criteria in sub-phase 6.3.
#
# Install manually in a development/VM environment for testing:
#   apt-get install labwc xdg-desktop-portal-wlr mako-notifier swaylock \
#                   swayidle kanshi grim slurp layer-shell-qt \
#                   qml6-module-org-kde-layershell
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Compositor ---
# libwlroots1x / libwlroots-0.xx is a dependency of labwc and is pulled in
# automatically; we do not list it explicitly here to avoid pinning to a
# specific SONAME that will change across Debian point releases.
labwc

# --- Qt6 layer-shell integration (for panel/dock/launcher surfaces) ---
# layer-shell-qt provides the Qt Wayland shell integration plugin and
# the org.kde.layershell QML module that lets our PyQt6 shell become a
# proper wlr-layer-shell surface. Required for panels/docks that reserve
# an exclusive zone (no overlapping with maximized windows).
layer-shell-qt
qml6-module-org-kde-layershell

# --- XDG portals (file dialogs, screenshots, screencast) ---
# xdg-desktop-portal-wlr provides the wlroots-specific screencopy/screenshot
# backend; xdg-desktop-portal-gtk is already in core for file dialogs.
xdg-desktop-portal-wlr

# --- Notifications daemon (lightweight, Wayland-native) ---
mako-notifier

# --- Screen lock / idle ---
swaylock
swayidle

# --- Output management (HiDPI / multi-monitor profiles) ---
kanshi

# --- Screenshot helpers ---
grim
slurp

# --- Polkit agent: policykit-1-gnome is already in core.list.chroot ---

# --- Optional: Lightweight terminal/file manager fallbacks for Lite ---
# foot is a Wayland-native terminal emulator; not strictly required if
# bright-terminal has its own Wayland client. Listed for reference.
# foot
